   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Photodiode"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "A photodiode is a p-n junction operated in reverse bias with a window or lens that lets light reach the junction. In the dark only a tiny dark current flows. Photons with energy above E_g create electron–hole pairs near the junction; the field sweeps them across, so the reverse current rises almost in proportion to the light intensity. Photodiodes are used in light meters, remote-control receivers, optical-fibre receivers and smoke detectors."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Reverse biased"
    },
    {
     "en": "Reverse current ∝ light intensity"
    },
    {
     "en": "Used in detectors and receivers"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "A photodiode is reverse biased. Light makes electron–hole pairs at the junction, so the reverse current rises with the light intensity.",
    "kn": "ಫೋಟೋಡಯೋಡ್ ಹಿಮ್ಮುಖ ಬಯಾಸ್‌ನಲ್ಲಿರುತ್ತದೆ. ಬೆಳಕು ಸಂಧಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ಎಲೆಕ್ಟ್ರಾನ್-ರಂಧ್ರ ಜೋಡಿಗಳನ್ನು ಉಂಟುಮಾಡಿ ಹಿಮ್ಮುಖ ಪ್ರವಾಹ ಬೆಳಕಿನ ತೀವ್ರತೆಯೊಂದಿಗೆ ಹೆಚ್ಚುತ್ತದೆ."
   }
