  {
   "id": "ex1",
   "type": "example",
   "title": {
    "en": "Worked example"
   },
   "problem": {
    "en": "A red LED (V_F = 2 V) is to glow at 15 mA from a 5 V supply. Find the series resistor and the power it dissipates."
   },
   "steps": [
    {
     "en": "Voltage across R = V_S − V_F = 5 − 2 = 3 V."
    },
    {
     "en": "R = 3 V / 0.015 A = 200 Ω."
    },
    {
     "en": "P = V × I = 3 × 0.015 = 0.045 W = 45 mW, so a ¼ W resistor is enough."
    }
   ],
   "answer": {
    "en": "R = 200 Ω; 45 mW"
   },
   "narration": {
